# Data lives outside the repo (bind-mounted over data/ in the devcontainer).
# Nothing under data/ is committed, so this needs no exceptions. Anything the
# repo does ship for a run lives outside data/ -- see examples/ and docs/data.md.
data/

# Metric CSVs from the training notebook. config.yaml sends these to
# paths.metrics_dir (under data/, already ignored above); this second net
# catches copies written anywhere else, e.g. by an older notebook run.
classification_report_*.csv

# Notebook / Python cruft
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.env

# Build metadata from `pip install -e .`
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Model bundle: no bundle is committed -- notebook 01 writes it (see
# models/example_model_v1/README.md). Ignore every model directory, then
# re-admit models/example_model_v1/ but ignore its contents, then whitelist the
# two documents that do ship. A fresh clone therefore gets the directory and an
# explanation of what belongs in it, while a trained bundle -- model.keras,
# scaler.pkl, label_maps.json, wavelengths.json and the best_weights.weights.h5
# by-product -- stays ignored and cannot be committed by accident. Anything new
# that training writes here is ignored by default; add a whitelist line only if
# you actually mean to commit it.
models/*
!models/example_model_v1/
models/example_model_v1/*
!models/example_model_v1/README.md
!models/example_model_v1/model_card.md
